From: UniFi reverse engineering <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] gpex: disable incompatible child migration state for multi-host machines

The standalone UDM Pro machine creates two generic PCIe host bridges. Their
synthetic root devices do not yet have a supported migration ABI.

---
 hw/pci-host/gpex.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hw/pci-host/gpex.c b/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
index 5fca7e39fb..0000000000 100644
--- a/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
+++ b/hw/pci-host/gpex.c
@@ -245,4 +245,3 @@ static void gpex_root_class_init(ObjectClass *klass, const void *data)
     set_bit(DEVICE_CATEGORY_BRIDGE, dc->categories);
     dc->desc = "QEMU generic PCIe host bridge";
-    dc->vmsd = &vmstate_gpex_root;
     k->vendor_id = PCI_VENDOR_ID_REDHAT;
